From 77e6f998f41161bb5867770a4e9c9fef805e8428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:28:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] asahi/hk: prototype VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix on the
 SIMD-group matrix FMA

The G13 ISA has simd_matrix_fmadd16/32 (dougallj/applegpu): an 8x8x8
SIMD-group multiply-accumulate where every operand is a register pair per
lane holding two elements of a tile, in the layout Metal's simdgroup_matrix
uses (metal-flash-attention morton_order, Apple patent US11256518B2).

* agx: new simd_matrix_fmadd opcode (8-byte SIMD-family encoding, bit 26
  selects the 32-bit variant, set from the accumulator size at pack time),
  register-pair read/write counts, emit from a new cmat_muladd_agx intrinsic.
* nir: cmat_muladd_agx (vec2 x vec2 x vec2 -> vec2 per lane).
* hk: hk_nir_lower_cooperative_matrix (from panvk's pass): everything is
  split into 8x8 tiles by nir_lower_cooperative_matrix_flexible_dimensions,
  cmat types become per-lane 2-vectors, loads/stores address the morton
  layout, muladd -> cmat_muladd_agx. Mixed f16 x f16 + f32 widens A and B to
  f32 (exact) and uses the f32 instruction (HK_CMAT_MIXED=1 tries the raw
  mixed encoding instead, for experiments).
* hk: advertise VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix (compute) with 16x16x16 and 8x8x8
  f16/f16/f32, f16/f16/f16 and f32/f32/f32 subgroup-scope shapes.

Tested on the M1 (G13G) with a standalone Vulkan test: all shapes and
layouts bit-exact against a CPU reference.

